# Credentials. Never commit these.
#
# `.env.*` is deliberately broad — it catches .env.local, .env.production, the .env.bak.* a careless
# edit leaves behind, and whatever variant someone invents next. The one exception is the template,
# which carries names and no values and has to stay tracked for `cp .env.example .env` to mean
# anything; the negation must sit after the wildcard or the wildcard wins.
#
# Note this file only protects what is not yet tracked. `git rm --cached` is what removes something
# already committed, and a secret that has been pushed is compromised regardless — rotate it rather
# than tidying up the history.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.credentials.json
**/.credentials.json
secrets.json
*.secret
.npmrc
.netrc
# Private keys and certificates, wherever they land in the tree.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*

# Claude Code local state. `settings.local.json` is this machine's permission grant and
# `.credentials.json` is the login itself; neither belongs to anyone but this checkout. A shared
# `.claude/settings.json` stays committable, so the rules name the local files rather than the
# directory.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json
.claude/.credentials.json
CLAUDE.md

# Runtime data. `var/` holds the database, the dataset and the venv; the database stores the NAMES of
# credential environment variables and never their values, but the tree is machine-local either way.
# The loose database globs are belt and braces: `--var-dir` can put the file anywhere.
var/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.db

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/

# JavaScript
node_modules/

# Build products
dist/
build/
*.bun-build

# Logs
*.log

# OS and editor droppings
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
